// Every construct of the document language, in one file.
document title: "Golden", author: "A. N. Author and B. Writer"
date "1 January 2026"
language en-GB

define brand as "tekx"
define cite(who, year = "2026") as "{who} ({year})"
define block warning(title = "Warning")
  quote
    **{title}.** {body}
define axiom2 like theorem titled "Postulate"

abstract
  A short abstract with *emphasis*, **strength**, `code` and a {brand} macro.

# Headings with hashes #h1

Paragraphs are separated by blank lines.^[A footnote with *emphasis*, $x^2$ and [brackets].]
A line break inside a paragraph is a space -- and dashes, quotes "like these",
ellipses... and non~breaking spaces become real typography.
See {cite(Knuth)} and {cite(Lamport, 1994)}.

## A subsection

- bullets
- with *inline* $x$ math
  1. nested
  2. ordered

1) parenthesized
2) numbers

> A quotation
> over two lines.

warning "Careful"
  The macro wraps this body.

axiom2 "Choice" #choice
  Every family of nonempty sets has a choice function.

theorem do
Written with do and end.
end

proof "Proof of everything"
  Trivial.

section* Unnumbered

| Left | Center | Right |
|:-----|:------:|------:|
| a    | $b$    | `c`   |

```
verbatim {brand} // not a comment
```

let f: RR -> RR be smooth

Links: <https://example.org>, [text](https://example.org/x), https://example.org/y, @choice, @h1.

references
  knuth: D. E. Knuth, *The TeXbook*, 1984.
  lamport: L. Lamport, *LaTeX*, 1994.
